      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\n// helper said wait / skip / still-there (the 'still there?' note is queued in the outbox; the poller posts it) -> stop quietly\nconst p = $json || {}, st = $('Start').first().json;\nif (!p.ok_to_run) return st.dry_run ? [{ json: { stop: true, dry_run: true, action: p.action || '', why_not: p.why_not || 'helper down', still_there: p.still_there || '', plan: p.plan_label } }] : [];\nconst reads = p.reads || [];\nif (!reads.length) return [{ json: { read: false, none: true } }];\nif (st.fake) return reads.map(r => ({ json: { read: false, spec: r } }));            // tests: fake posts / targets, no browser\nconst handle = 'your_x_handle';\nreturn reads.map(r => ({ json: { read: true, spec: r, task: (r.type === 'x_search' || r.type === 'x_watch' || r.type === 'x_following')\n  ? `Open ${r.url} . READ-ONLY task on X ${r.type === 'x_watch' ? 'watchlist (from:handles)' : r.type === 'x_following' ? 'Following/Home' : 'results'} (logged in as @${handle}; do not like, reply, follow, repost or click any button).\nWait for the posts to load. Use the extract action once to read the first 10 posts (scroll down once only if fewer than 6 are visible).\nFor each post get: url (its permalink https://x.com/<handle>/status/<id>, from the post's timestamp link), handle, text (full post text), age (e.g. 25m, 3h).\nSkip promoted/ad posts. Then call done with ONLY a JSON array of these posts and nothing else.`\n  : `Open ${r.url} . READ-ONLY: read this one ${r.platform === 'facebook' ? 'Facebook' : 'LinkedIn'} post. Do not like, react, comment, share, follow, connect or click any button.\nIf a sign-in page, captcha, security checkpoint, 'unusual activity' or any warning appears, STOP and call done with success=false and text starting 'STOPPED:'.\nOtherwise call done with ONLY this JSON: {\"author\": \"<name>\", \"text\": \"<the post text, max 800 characters>\"}` } }));\n"
      }
